From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:07:07 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: smd-rpm: Release unused handoff votes in the sleep
 set

The handoff at probe votes every RPM clock on in both the active and the
sleep set, and nothing ever withdraws the votes of clocks no consumer
claims: without an .is_prepared op, clk_disable_unused() skips them. On
MSM8996 that leaves the XO buffers (BB_CLK1/2, RF_CLK1/2, DIV_CLK1-3),
IPA, CE1 and QDSS in the APSS sleep set for good, and the RPM never shuts
the XO down even though every master releases it.

Count the handoff vote as an enable and report the clocks that vote in
the sleep set as prepared, so clk_disable_unused() releases the unused
ones. Active-only clocks get a sleep vote of 0 at handoff and are never
reported prepared: what is on while the APSS is awake does not change.
(Releasing the active-only halves too made the USB2 PHY's PLL fail to
lock at resume after XO shutdown.)

Tested on the SM-T820: with this and the MDP5 bandwidth fix, a 60 s
s2idle on battery spends 61 s in RPM vmin (it never did before) and USB
resumes (test DT with cluster/system power collapse and MPM, PCIe off,
board without panel; Wi-Fi and display resume not covered yet).

Similar to Konrad Dybcio's unmerged "SMD RPMCC sleep preparations"
(.is_prepared hook by Shawn Guo).

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/clk-smd-rpm.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-smd-rpm.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-smd-rpm.c
index 487d715ed5..7281df0d57 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-smd-rpm.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-smd-rpm.c
@@ -201,6 +201,15 @@ static int clk_smd_rpm_handoff(const struct clk_smd_rpm *r)
 				 sizeof(req));
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * An active-only clock never needs the resource while the APSS
+	 * sleeps; voting for it in the sleep set would keep the RPM from
+	 * shutting the XO down.
+	 */
+	if (r->active_only)
+		req.value = 0;
+
 	ret = qcom_rpm_smd_write(rpmcc_smd_rpm, QCOM_SMD_RPM_SLEEP_STATE,
 				 r->rpm_res_type, r->rpm_clk_id, &req,
 				 sizeof(req));
@@ -412,9 +421,25 @@ static int clk_smd_rpm_enable_scaling(void)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The handoff vote at probe leaves every clock on. Reporting the clocks that
+ * vote in the sleep set as prepared lets clk_disable_unused() release the
+ * ones no consumer claimed, so that they don't keep the RPM from shutting
+ * the XO down. Active-only clocks are never reported prepared: their handoff
+ * vote (active set only) stays, so what is on while the APSS is awake does
+ * not change.
+ */
+static int clk_smd_rpm_is_prepared(struct clk_hw *hw)
+{
+	struct clk_smd_rpm *r = to_clk_smd_rpm(hw);
+
+	return r->enabled && !r->active_only;
+}
+
 static const struct clk_ops clk_smd_rpm_ops = {
 	.prepare	= clk_smd_rpm_prepare,
 	.unprepare	= clk_smd_rpm_unprepare,
+	.is_prepared	= clk_smd_rpm_is_prepared,
 	.set_rate	= clk_smd_rpm_set_rate,
 	.determine_rate = clk_determine_rate_noop,
 	.recalc_rate	= clk_smd_rpm_recalc_rate,
@@ -423,6 +448,7 @@ static const struct clk_ops clk_smd_rpm_ops = {
 static const struct clk_ops clk_smd_rpm_branch_ops = {
 	.prepare	= clk_smd_rpm_prepare,
 	.unprepare	= clk_smd_rpm_unprepare,
+	.is_prepared	= clk_smd_rpm_is_prepared,
 	.recalc_rate	= clk_smd_rpm_recalc_rate,
 };
 
@@ -1365,6 +1391,9 @@ static int rpm_smd_clk_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		ret = clk_smd_rpm_handoff(rpm_smd_clks[i]);
 		if (ret)
 			goto err;
+
+		/* The handoff vote is on until a consumer releases it */
+		rpm_smd_clks[i]->enabled = true;
 	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < desc->num_icc_clks; i++) {
